1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:05,197
This love in my heart,
it will burn on forever.

2
00:00:05,280 --> 00:00:09,037
Granting me courage, I
hope it will never stop.

3
00:00:09,120 --> 00:00:12,177
No matter where you
are, nothing is too far.

4
00:00:12,260 --> 00:00:15,857
With our everlasting bones,
we'll reach it, we are home.

5
00:00:15,940 --> 00:00:22,637
I'm

6
00:00:22,720 --> 00:00:23,917
so truly grateful.

7
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,820
I ran into you on that day so long ago.

8
00:00:28,740 --> 00:00:32,397
We laughed every moment
with tears in our eyes.

9
00:00:32,480 --> 00:00:34,860
Till we knew we weren't alone.

10
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:41,820
The blowing wind came in
and joined us on our way.

11
00:00:43,220 --> 00:00:47,097
And with it I know we'll rise.

12
00:00:47,180 --> 00:00:49,797
We'll be flying up high.

13
00:00:49,880 --> 00:00:52,900
Why, tell me why are you giving up?

14
00:00:53,460 --> 00:00:56,120
Why, tell me why you want to fight alone?

15
00:00:56,720 --> 00:00:59,620
Hey, what kind of future
do you think you have?

16
00:00:59,880 --> 00:01:03,197
Your dream is already in your hands.

17
00:01:03,280 --> 00:01:06,937
This love in my heart,
it will burn off forever.

18
00:01:07,020 --> 00:01:10,757
Granting me courage, I
hope it will never stop.

19
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:13,897
I don't matter where you
are, nothing is too far.

20
00:01:13,980 --> 00:01:17,637
With our everlasting possible
reaching, we are home.

21
00:01:17,720 --> 00:01:20,537
From the horizon, out on
the edge of the world.

22
00:01:20,620 --> 00:01:23,477
There is a place that
I want to take you to.

23
00:01:23,560 --> 00:01:24,897
Let's head for it then.

24
00:01:24,980 --> 00:01:28,440
But as for the way, we already know.

25
00:01:29,260 --> 00:01:31,600
We promised it long ago.

26
00:01:43,360 --> 00:01:45,317
You scream by your voice.

27
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:47,237
That can't break through the silence.

28
00:01:47,320 --> 00:01:48,817
Feeling defeated.

29
00:01:48,900 --> 00:01:51,037
It crushes your helpless heart.

30
00:01:51,120 --> 00:01:52,697
I've got your back, I swear.

31
00:01:52,780 --> 00:01:54,177
I'll always be here.

32
00:01:54,260 --> 00:01:57,960
Let's put our fate within
this light under the sun.

33
00:01:58,960 --> 00:02:02,880
Can you close your eyes and
just listen to my voice?

34
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:05,097
Let's find the answer together.

35
00:02:05,180 --> 00:02:07,597
I'm telling you in our path.

36
00:02:07,680 --> 00:02:09,617
I trust that it will lead us.

37
00:02:09,700 --> 00:02:11,517
To another sea untarded.

38
00:02:11,600 --> 00:02:13,437
Cause now we are home.

39
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:16,197
On the horizon, out on
the edge of the world.

40
00:02:16,280 --> 00:02:19,197
There is a place that
I want to take you to.

41
00:02:19,280 --> 00:02:20,697
Let's head for it then.

42
00:02:20,780 --> 00:02:24,140
But after the way, we already know.

43
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:27,280
We promised it long ago.

44
00:02:36,900 --> 00:02:38,560
What was that ruckus?

45
00:02:38,740 --> 00:02:42,446
I heard a loud noise coming from
over there Was it an intruder?

46
00:02:44,840 --> 00:02:45,780
Is that it?

47
00:02:48,060 --> 00:02:49,825
What the hell's going on here?

48
00:02:51,820 --> 00:02:54,160
Bobbin, sir, what happened to the wall?

49
00:02:57,540 --> 00:02:59,658
Don't tell us you were under attack.

50
00:03:00,040 --> 00:03:01,417
Did somebody try to hurt you?

51
00:03:01,500 --> 00:03:07,600
It was nothing unusual, but rest
assured, you can all take it easy.

52
00:03:10,500 --> 00:03:11,380
Bobbin, sir.

53
00:03:23,900 --> 00:03:25,800
There's no need to worry.

54
00:03:26,260 --> 00:03:29,500
I can take care of this
little problem myself.

55
00:03:30,080 --> 00:03:32,380
He won't get away with this.

56
00:03:32,560 --> 00:03:33,960
I swear it!

57
00:03:34,640 --> 00:03:38,577
Even the demons from
Hell itself wouldn't dare

58
00:03:38,660 --> 00:03:42,240
turn down an invitation
to Mama's Tea Party.

59
00:03:48,500 --> 00:03:49,837
Magic Mirror!

60
00:03:49,920 --> 00:03:51,120
Thank you, Tia.

61
00:03:51,480 --> 00:03:52,560
You're welcome.

62
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:59,500
Hey, uh, I think there's
something right behind Brooke.

63
00:04:05,620 --> 00:04:07,080
It can't be.

64
00:04:11,540 --> 00:04:13,440
This will be quite troublesome.

65
00:04:22,440 --> 00:04:27,600
So what's the plan if
you need it spelled out.

66
00:04:30,900 --> 00:04:34,157
That mirror leads to mama's bedroom.

67
00:04:34,240 --> 00:04:37,877
So that's one of the emperors of the sea.

68
00:04:37,960 --> 00:04:42,340
At the very least he's still alive.

69
00:04:43,440 --> 00:04:44,620
This will be messy.

70
00:04:44,880 --> 00:04:46,800
Why is he there of all places?

71
00:04:50,160 --> 00:04:52,520
Yeah, why is she sleeping with him?

72
00:04:54,340 --> 00:04:56,860
He seems to be deep in slumber himself.

73
00:04:57,300 --> 00:04:58,960
How can he relax right now?

74
00:04:59,200 --> 00:05:00,980
Hey, Brock, wake up!

75
00:05:04,460 --> 00:05:05,520
No use.

76
00:05:05,760 --> 00:05:07,584
Guess he can't hear you at all.

77
00:05:09,260 --> 00:05:12,157
Good luck trying to
get Mama to let him go.

78
00:05:12,240 --> 00:05:14,660
She adores oddities like him.

79
00:05:14,860 --> 00:05:16,300
But don't fret.

80
00:05:17,040 --> 00:05:20,099
I can help you out by making
her loosen up her grip.

81
00:05:20,340 --> 00:05:21,500
Hey, Mama!

82
00:05:22,180 --> 00:05:24,620
It's me, Barrel! Chouchou!

83
00:05:24,980 --> 00:05:26,060
Chouchou!

84
00:05:26,520 --> 00:05:27,460
Knock it out!

85
00:05:27,800 --> 00:05:28,780
Silence them!

86
00:05:29,380 --> 00:05:30,280
Let's go!

87
00:05:38,700 --> 00:05:40,960
Hey, do you think she heard us?

88
00:05:41,080 --> 00:05:41,940
Is she awake?

89
00:05:45,600 --> 00:05:47,660
Good. Still out cold.

90
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:54,880
She, she, she knows that we're here.

91
00:05:55,660 --> 00:05:56,490
Oh,

92
00:05:56,573 --> 00:06:03,360
I

93
00:06:03,980 --> 00:06:04,810
see.

94
00:06:04,893 --> 00:06:05,780
Just a fly.

95
00:06:18,440 --> 00:06:20,080
What? Who's there? The boy?

96
00:06:21,140 --> 00:06:22,220
Uh, he's up!

97
00:06:22,540 --> 00:06:24,680
Bear, can you hear us?

98
00:06:24,800 --> 00:06:25,880
We're over here!

99
00:06:30,260 --> 00:06:32,280
Oh, I see. That's fine.

100
00:06:33,900 --> 00:06:34,800
The freak?

101
00:06:35,700 --> 00:06:37,580
Huh? What, Mama?

102
00:06:38,300 --> 00:06:39,418
We're under attack?

103
00:06:39,720 --> 00:06:42,560
I need my freak! You'll go! Hey!

104
00:06:46,220 --> 00:06:47,620
There you are!

105
00:07:16,940 --> 00:07:19,040
Are they really that powerful?

106
00:07:32,120 --> 00:07:34,480
Who are we supposed to save him?

107
00:07:34,760 --> 00:07:37,280
He's just killing me!

108
00:07:39,160 --> 00:07:41,360
This looks grim!

109
00:07:56,120 --> 00:07:57,640
Hey, stop it!

110
00:07:57,880 --> 00:07:59,800
That food doesn't belong to you!

111
00:08:08,220 --> 00:08:09,700
I'm sorry, boy.

112
00:08:10,460 --> 00:08:14,166
But there's somebody really
important I've got to give this to.

113
00:08:23,320 --> 00:08:24,150
Hmm.

114
00:08:24,760 --> 00:08:27,054
I think this baby needs some more hair.

115
00:08:27,280 --> 00:08:28,280
How's this, then?

116
00:08:28,640 --> 00:08:30,620
Eating improvement? For sure.

117
00:08:30,940 --> 00:08:32,116
Way more convincing.

118
00:08:32,220 --> 00:08:34,197
Where did you even find this guy, anyway?

119
00:08:34,280 --> 00:08:36,456
He's from the execution grounds here.

120
00:08:36,860 --> 00:08:39,507
The Afro is made of
seaweed from the kitchen.

121
00:08:40,500 --> 00:08:42,912
All right, our friend here is good to go.

122
00:08:43,400 --> 00:08:46,900
Wow, he looks exactly like Brook. Totally.

123
00:08:47,400 --> 00:08:49,877
If we can just switch him
out with the real Brook,

124
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:52,057
I don't think she'll
even notice he's gone.

125
00:08:52,140 --> 00:08:52,970
Good work.

126
00:08:56,920 --> 00:09:00,040
Now if we place Barrel at
the midpoint between worlds,

127
00:09:00,360 --> 00:09:04,654
we should be able to easily enter and
exit the giant mirror as we please.

128
00:09:05,200 --> 00:09:06,030
Huh?

129
00:09:06,400 --> 00:09:08,060
Damn it, I'll make them pay.

130
00:09:09,700 --> 00:09:12,097
And with that, I believe
we're all set now.

131
00:09:12,180 --> 00:09:13,415
Shall we get to work?

132
00:09:14,200 --> 00:09:16,580
Let the Brook Rescue Mission commence!

133
00:09:19,120 --> 00:09:20,240
Challenge one!

134
00:09:21,660 --> 00:09:23,600
Wish me luck! Here I go!

135
00:09:23,800 --> 00:09:25,859
Remember, you can't make any noise.

136
00:09:26,040 --> 00:09:27,360
You can count on me!

137
00:09:41,120 --> 00:09:41,950
Ahhhh...

138
00:09:46,480 --> 00:09:48,580
Alright, wait for me, Brooke.

139
00:09:48,880 --> 00:09:49,720
I'm coming.

140
00:10:03,780 --> 00:10:04,917
Don't scream!

141
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:10,020
I was scared!

142
00:10:10,360 --> 00:10:12,000
So incredibly scared!

143
00:10:12,360 --> 00:10:13,780
Are you two okay?

144
00:10:14,220 --> 00:10:17,280
Somebody else needs to do it then. Let me!

145
00:10:17,480 --> 00:10:19,539
I'll make sure to get the job done!

146
00:10:20,660 --> 00:10:21,980
Challenge two!

147
00:10:29,660 --> 00:10:30,490
Oh!

148
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:32,140
That a girl!

149
00:10:32,740 --> 00:10:33,570
Brooke!

150
00:10:33,653 --> 00:10:34,680
Brooke, wake up!

151
00:10:35,040 --> 00:10:37,640
You gotta go, sleepyhead! Oh, no!

152
00:10:37,900 --> 00:10:41,040
The bubble is getting
bigger! Leave now! Ah!

153
00:10:48,220 --> 00:10:49,540
Did she notice?

154
00:10:53,960 --> 00:10:55,980
It's looking right at me.

155
00:11:02,440 --> 00:11:03,270
Huh?

156
00:11:03,400 --> 00:11:04,340
What'd you do?

157
00:11:04,580 --> 00:11:06,140
A stuffed bunny defense.

158
00:11:06,480 --> 00:11:07,774
I won't fall for that.

159
00:11:11,240 --> 00:11:12,600
Oh, never mind.

160
00:11:12,980 --> 00:11:15,120
I guess it's just a stuffed bunny.

161
00:11:17,080 --> 00:11:19,440
Wait, that really worked? Hurry!

162
00:11:19,620 --> 00:11:21,267
This is your chance, Carrot!

163
00:11:23,420 --> 00:11:25,120
I'll do it this time.

164
00:11:35,900 --> 00:11:37,840
It's that damn fly again.

165
00:11:38,180 --> 00:11:40,040
What an annoying pet!

166
00:11:48,900 --> 00:11:49,730
I'm scared!

167
00:11:50,040 --> 00:11:51,400
So incredibly scared!

168
00:11:52,720 --> 00:11:54,520
Alright, who's up next?

169
00:11:54,940 --> 00:11:56,646
What an embarrassing display.

170
00:11:56,840 --> 00:11:57,700
Very well.

171
00:11:58,140 --> 00:12:00,100
I guess it's up to me.

172
00:12:01,340 --> 00:12:02,540
Challenge three!

173
00:12:12,080 --> 00:12:12,910
Brooke!

174
00:12:13,260 --> 00:12:14,920
It's time to head out!

175
00:12:15,180 --> 00:12:16,040
Come on!

176
00:12:21,420 --> 00:12:22,920
She rolled over!

177
00:12:28,340 --> 00:12:29,600
Did that wake him?

178
00:12:30,400 --> 00:12:31,230
No.

179
00:12:31,540 --> 00:12:33,417
He's out of Big Mom's hands now.

180
00:12:33,500 --> 00:12:35,340
Okay, let me have a shot.

181
00:12:36,480 --> 00:12:37,540
Challenge four.

182
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:42,680
Brock! Hey, get up!

183
00:12:46,960 --> 00:12:47,860
Hiya, Brock!

184
00:12:48,900 --> 00:12:49,730
Huh?

185
00:12:49,813 --> 00:12:51,200
It's me, Nami!

186
00:12:57,280 --> 00:12:59,480
What now?

187
00:13:01,900 --> 00:13:03,280
Are you still here?

188
00:13:06,400 --> 00:13:07,880
Oh, no!

189
00:13:08,480 --> 00:13:11,260
I'm trying to save you stupid fly!

190
00:13:13,940 --> 00:13:15,040
Heavenly!

191
00:13:15,860 --> 00:13:16,960
Fire!

192
00:13:31,380 --> 00:13:32,820
Nice work!

193
00:13:37,500 --> 00:13:39,920
That was way too close.

194
00:13:41,680 --> 00:13:43,920
Jinbei, thank you.

195
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:47,235
Mission accomplished!

196
00:13:48,900 --> 00:13:49,730
Where?

197
00:13:49,840 --> 00:13:51,280
That was scary!

198
00:13:51,760 --> 00:13:52,960
Oh, man!

199
00:14:25,700 --> 00:14:28,540
It seems like you really
messed these guys up.

200
00:14:42,920 --> 00:14:44,960
Good thing you said your goodbyes.

201
00:14:48,240 --> 00:14:53,380
It turns out we're holding Straw Hat and
the Cat Burglar captive in the library.

202
00:14:54,140 --> 00:14:58,517
Luffy fought all night against one of
Big Mom's strongest generals to get here.

203
00:14:58,600 --> 00:15:00,877
He's in no shape to do this,

204
00:15:00,960 --> 00:15:06,140
Luffy, you told me you'd be waiting.

205
00:15:10,480 --> 00:15:12,220
Where the hell are you!

206
00:15:23,120 --> 00:15:24,400
Luffy!

207
00:15:26,140 --> 00:15:26,970
Luffy!

208
00:15:32,400 --> 00:15:33,680
Luffy!

209
00:15:34,260 --> 00:15:36,000
I'm utterly shocked!

210
00:15:39,080 --> 00:15:42,160
Ah, ah, ah, about everything!

211
00:15:43,120 --> 00:15:44,740
Do not have it, Dr. Speed!

212
00:15:48,220 --> 00:15:50,740
You picked the worst type thing out!

213
00:15:52,040 --> 00:15:53,960
I sincerely thank you.

214
00:15:54,760 --> 00:15:57,280
All that matters is that you're safe now.

215
00:15:57,900 --> 00:16:00,300
Yes, I thought I was dead for certain.

216
00:16:01,700 --> 00:16:03,420
Or rather, double dead.

217
00:16:07,460 --> 00:16:09,077
With the heightened security,

218
00:16:09,160 --> 00:16:11,697
I should have realized sooner
that we would be unable

219
00:16:11,780 --> 00:16:14,721
to make a copy of the Road
Poneglyph on this trip.

220
00:16:15,300 --> 00:16:17,100
It's my fault for pushing it.

221
00:16:17,360 --> 00:16:19,419
I needlessly put your life at risk.

222
00:16:20,460 --> 00:16:21,500
My apologies.

223
00:16:22,400 --> 00:16:23,600
Don't be ridiculous.

224
00:16:24,060 --> 00:16:26,531
You selflessly stuck your neck out for us.

225
00:16:27,560 --> 00:16:32,120
Had it not been for your bold idea
to infiltrate as a two-man team,

226
00:16:32,440 --> 00:16:35,264
we never would have had
this golden opportunity.

227
00:16:35,920 --> 00:16:39,677
If we attempted to take the stone
rubbings on any other occasion,

228
00:16:39,760 --> 00:16:43,500
there would have been no way
to avoid an Alto pirate war.

229
00:16:45,900 --> 00:16:47,280
We had to try.

230
00:16:47,740 --> 00:16:50,880
Despite the poor odds,
it was our only option.

231
00:16:57,400 --> 00:16:58,800
Here, the copy.

232
00:17:00,320 --> 00:17:04,496
Anyway, I can't tell you how glad I
am that you got away safely, Pedro.

233
00:17:05,020 --> 00:17:10,037
The copy I wish our plan hadn't
been so fraught with peril,

234
00:17:10,120 --> 00:17:13,777
but asking you to act as bait
was all I could scrape together.

235
00:17:13,860 --> 00:17:17,097
Hold on—is this what I think it is? Brook?

236
00:17:17,180 --> 00:17:19,577
It's a copy of the poneglyph.

237
00:17:19,660 --> 00:17:20,490
I

238
00:17:21,740 --> 00:17:27,017
made it with seconds to spare, just as
I finished transcribing the third sheet.

239
00:17:27,100 --> 00:17:31,020
sheet And out of the blue
came Big Mom herself.

240
00:17:35,240 --> 00:17:37,320
I can't believe our eyes!

241
00:17:41,460 --> 00:17:43,297
You Karoo got past all the guards?

242
00:17:43,380 --> 00:17:45,968
You even got past all
of the sweet generals?

243
00:17:49,880 --> 00:17:53,617
Do you Karoo even know
what the other emperors of

244
00:17:53,700 --> 00:17:55,877
the sea would do to get
their hands on her road,

245
00:17:55,960 --> 00:17:56,790
Poneglyph?

246
00:17:57,540 --> 00:17:59,160
And this is it?

247
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:04,140
Um, yes.

248
00:18:06,640 --> 00:18:07,470
What?

249
00:18:08,080 --> 00:18:11,860
He not only reached, but
copied our poneglyph?

250
00:18:18,740 --> 00:18:20,260
A miracle!

251
00:18:21,840 --> 00:18:22,670
Oftentimes,

252
00:18:23,020 --> 00:18:27,608
even Big Mom's own beloved family is not
permitted in the treasure repository.

253
00:18:27,940 --> 00:18:29,860
You really are something else!

254
00:18:30,340 --> 00:18:32,900
Perhaps now I'm worthy of a panty-peak?

255
00:18:34,100 --> 00:18:34,930
Hey!

256
00:18:35,013 --> 00:18:36,120
He's already hurt!

257
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:37,830
Amazing!

258
00:18:37,940 --> 00:18:40,477
That takes care of one
of our big objectives!

259
00:18:40,560 --> 00:18:43,640
That means all that's left
is for us to grab Sanji!

260
00:18:58,060 --> 00:19:00,860
Thank you.

261
00:19:27,840 --> 00:19:29,600
No one knows where they are!

262
00:19:29,780 --> 00:19:30,620
Sorry, miss!

263
00:19:30,960 --> 00:19:33,480
They did pass by me a while ago, though.

264
00:19:33,660 --> 00:19:35,177
Yeah, but they're off here now!

265
00:19:35,260 --> 00:19:36,557
What about Sanji's room?

266
00:19:36,640 --> 00:19:39,877
No, just some weird guy that's
made himself quite comfortable.

267
00:19:39,960 --> 00:19:40,790
That's it.

268
00:19:41,200 --> 00:19:42,788
I think I know where he is.

269
00:19:43,440 --> 00:19:46,264
He has to be outside where
there are no mirrors.

270
00:19:46,540 --> 00:19:49,280
And just earlier, Luffy
met Sanji in a field.

271
00:19:52,140 --> 00:19:53,787
And they got in a big fight.

272
